The bartender nods with a smile, and begins pouring your drinks. No waitress yet tonight, which makes sense at this time. He brings the beers directly to you, opening a tab.
The two of you drink for a while, talking about work and the recent Sports Festival, until your friend points out a dart board across the room.
She raises her brows in challenge, and you can do nothing but accept.
Bellemere: Alright! Winner pays for drinks!
You had a feeling it would turn out like this. You laugh, but nod.
