title: date_bellemere_3_play_1
location: bar
---

You do your very best, playing through the game with legs shoulder-width apart, aiming for the big points. Since it’s only a 301-point game, it goes fast. You’re not too far behind, since the game is short, but you’re not winning. Bellemere, predictably, gets close to the end first, and since she needs only four points to end the game she just needed to hit a double 2 in the outer ring.
Such a tiny little block of red; she was on her second try, and swore when she barely missed.
Bellemere: Too much beer, I think!
{$name}: Oh? Excuses?
Bellemere gives you a surprised look, then shakes her head.
Bellemere: Oh, you’re in for it now! Just wait!
Teasing aside, the short game actually means it’s quite close. On your next turn, you come up to the end point on your own game. If Bellemere fails her next turn, and you hit a double 20 on your own, you could win…
Unfortunately, you’re not that lucky. She hits her mark, and jumps up in victory.
Bellemere: WOOO! In your FACE, {$name}!
She is not a very gracious winner.
Bellemere: Good show though, overall. I’m impressed!
Okay, so… maybe you didn’t win, but with the redhead’s kind words, it still feels like it.
<<jump date_bellemere_3_dance>>
