You find Soul King Brook’s music rather soulful and blood-pumping, even if the guy is(technically) a pirate. You’ve been a fan for a while now, and you hope Bellemere won’t judge your taste in music too harshly.
Bellemere: Hey, I love this guy! He’s got a jazzy beat… like, what a voice! Lots of exclamations. He must be fun at parties!
{$name}: I hear he’s literally the living dead.
Bellemere: I know; isn’t it cool?
Ah, so she’s a fan, too? 
You grin, holding out a hand for the Commodore, and she takes it eagerly. Before you can lead her to the dance floor she leaps forward, pulling you behind roughly and turning you in a full circle with a laugh.
The two of you dance- not *well*, but with a sudden enthusiasm brought on by good music and drinks.
You end the night exhausted from so much partying, both promising to do it again sometime. 
